# Git commits

- **Format:** Conventional Commits — `type(scope): subject`
  - Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `perf`, `ci`, etc.
  - Subject: short, imperative, **why**-focused (not a file list).
  - Body optional; keep it brief when used.
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` (or similar) trailers for Cursor, Cursor agent, Composer, or any AI/tool.
- **Never** update git config (`user.name`, `user.email`, aliases, etc.).
- Do not amend, `--no-verify`, force-push, or push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never commit `.env` or secrets; use `.env.example` as the template.

```text
# ✅ GOOD
feat(security): key rate limits by user id and disable by default

# ❌ BAD — AI trailer
feat(security): key rate limits by user id
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```
